Stores imported or manually entered bank statements with lines for reconciling bank transactions against the company’s accounting records.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Import bank statements (CSV, OFX, QIF, CAMT, etc.)
Manual entry of daily bank transactions
Bank reconciliation (match statement lines with journal items)
Handle fees, interest, direct debits, and transfers
Cash management and daily cash position
Multi-currency bank accounts and foreign currency gain/loss

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread)
Key Fields:
name (char, sequenced), journal_id (→ account.journal, required)
date (date), balance_start, balance_end_real, balance_end
state (selection: open / posted / confirm)
One2many: line_ids → account.bank.statement.line
currency_id, company_id
Computed: total_amount, difference

Critical Hooks:
button_post, button_validate, action_reconcile
_compute_balance_end, reconcile_bank_line
import wizards heavily linked

Security: account.group_account_manager + bank journal access rules
Workflow: Open → Posted → Reconciled; strong integration with account.payment and account.move

RAG Routing Keywords:
bank statement, bank reconciliation, statement line, reconcile bank, imported statement, bank feed, cash book, bank balance, statement import, CODA, MT940, CAMT.053, bank extract, unreconciled transaction
Related Models (most joined):

account.bank.statement.line (main child)
account.journal (bank journal)
account.move.line (via reconciliation)
account.payment
res.partner (for counterpart)
account.account (liquidity account)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.bank.statement holds complete bank statements linked to a bank journal with starting/ending balance, statement lines, and reconciliation status. It is the core model for bank statement import, manual entry, automatic reconciliation with journal items or payments, and daily cash management. Heavily used together with account.bank.statement.line, account.journal, and account.move.line for full bank reconciliation flow in Odoo accounting.